I've implemented the node, but left out both operations requests: the log-file append and the metadata fetch. This node can't do either safely, so they need to be raised with whoever owns the graph.

- **The log file:** the target is `wasm32-unknown-unknown` with no WASI adapter, so the component has no filesystem. Writing a log file would mean importing a filesystem capability. That would either fail to link on the host or give the node authority the graph doesn't grant it.
- **The metadata fetch:** the node holds only `DBHandle<'knowledge-base', read>`. Importing `aap:caps/http-client` would add network access the graph never granted. It would also send the customer's untrusted question text to an outside service.

If operations needs these, a separate host-tier node or a host-side tap can provide them. That would need its own capabilities declared in the graph, so the validator can check it.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{moderated-query, conversation-context};

    import aap:caps/kb-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(query: moderated-query) -> conversation-context;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::kb_read;

const MAX_QUESTION_CHARS: usize = 512;
const NO_KNOWLEDGE: &str = "No relevant knowledge-base entries were found for this question.";

struct Node;

/// Bound the question to MAX_QUESTION_CHARS characters. The `requires` clause
/// already guarantees this, so this is a no-op on valid input; it keeps the
/// `ensures len(question) <= 512` clause true by construction.
fn bound_question(q: String) -> String {
    if q.chars().count() <= MAX_QUESTION_CHARS {
        q
    } else {
        q.chars().take(MAX_QUESTION_CHARS).collect()
    }
}

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(query: ModeratedQuery) -> ConversationContext {
        let inner = query.query;
        let intent = inner.intent;
        let question = bound_question(inner.question);

        // Read-only lookup against the knowledge base: the only capability this
        // node holds. Operations' log-file append and metadata HTTP fetch are
        // deliberately not implemented: this component has no filesystem
        // (wasm32-unknown-unknown, no WASI) and is not granted http-client.
        let mut knowledge: Vec<String> = kb_read::lookup(&question)
            .into_iter()
            .filter(|s| !s.trim().is_empty())
            .collect();

        // ensures present(knowledge): never hand downstream an empty list.
        if knowledge.is_empty() {
            knowledge.push(NO_KNOWLEDGE.to_string());
        }

        ConversationContext {
            intent,
            question,
            knowledge,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

